  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 拍\ntitle: clap; musical beat\njlpt: 1\ntags: [jlpt-n1, grade-8, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 8\nradical: 手\nradicalNumber: 64\nonyomi: [ハク, ヒョウ]\nkunyomi: []\nquizOnyomi: [ハク]\nquizKunyomi: []\ndistractors: [古, 右, 川]\nquiz_exclusions: [打, 当, 撃, 批, 触, 接, 抵, 摩, 擦, 律, 調, 整, 楽, 曲, 音, 木, 板, 盤, 析, 刻, 時, 動, 印, 標, 点, 書, 著, 送, 伝, 寄, 輸, 入, 注, 結, 括, 投, 払, 給, 作, 造, 備, 設, 演, 耕, 訪, 伺, 参, 励, 勧, 賛, 騒, 突, 鳴, 勉, 勇, 乗, 記, 識, 筆, 響]\n---\n\n# 拍 — clap; musical beat\n\n**Strokes:** 8 · **Key (radical):** 手 (no. 64) · **JLPT:** N1 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n拍 concerns striking or clapping and keeping a beat. In\n[拍手](../words/拍手.md) はくしゅ it contributes the clapping action,\nwhile 手 identifies the hands. The noun 拍 はく can name a musical beat\nand, in linguistics, a mora. A mora is a timing unit, not necessarily\nthe same unit as a syllable.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic, not etymology:** imagine the hand-shaped 扌\nbeside 白 keeping a visible beat. The indexing radical is 手; 扌 is its\nleft-side form. This invented picture is not an account of the early character.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Kind | Example or disposition |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ハク | on | [拍手](../words/拍手.md) はくしゅ, clapping or applause; the linked article supports this practice reading. |\n| ヒョウ | on | 拍子 ひょうし, musical time or rhythm. This verified whole-word example has no linked support article here, so ヒョウ is recognition material. |\n\nThe full ハク・ヒョウ inventory and empty kun list remain unchanged.\n字通 separately records うつ・たたく・はやし, and Weblio's Wiktionary\nsection includes ヒャク. These source-positive supplemental forms are\nnot additional selected practice readings.\n\n## Common words\n\n- [拍手](../words/拍手.md) はくしゅ - applause; clapping, also ritual\n  hand-clapping in the appropriate context.\n- 拍子 ひょうし - musical time, rhythm or beat; its moment/chance senses\n  belong to the whole word.\n- 心拍 しんぱく - heartbeat. The contextual ぱく does not replace ハク\n  in the full character-reading inventory.\n\n## Notes\n\n- JMdict places 拍つ うつ in the complete 打つ/拍つ/搏つ/撲つ/擣つ\n  family and flags the 拍つ spelling as rarely used. That family also\n  contains sending, marking, injecting, throwing, paying, making,\n  performing, visiting and other senses without an explicit allocation\n  to every spelling. They remain source evidence, not a recommendation\n  to replace ordinary 打つ with 拍つ in all of them. Conservative direct\n  guards protect the unresolved broad choices; they do not assert that\n  bare 拍 ordinarily means each action.\n- [記](記.md), [識](識.md) and [筆](筆.md) also receive direct\n  precautions for that family's unallocated writing/marking senses.\n  識 has a real secondary writing sense, not only knowledge, and 筆\n  names writing as well as the implement. These guards do not establish\n  ordinary bare 拍 as a replacement for writing verbs.\n- 字通 also gives keeping time, cheering and wooden clappers. Complete\n  comparison families record wooden clappers under [木](木.md), and\n  under search-only 析 in the 柝 family. [板](板.md), [盤](盤.md) and\n  the broad music/time labels receive precautions too. A clapper is\n  not all wood, and a beat is not a fixed number of seconds.\n- [打](打.md), [撃](撃.md) and [当](当.md) include striking.\n  [突](突.md) also has 突く つく, to hit or strike, beyond thrusting\n  and suddenness; its direct guard does not equate every thrust with\n  clapping. [鳴](鳴.md)'s 鳴らす ならす includes beating or snapping\n  fingers. [響](響.md) concerns sound carrying or resonating rather\n  than the clapping action or a musical pulse. Its effect/impression\n  senses also meet the complete 打つ/rare 拍つ family's\n  move/impress/touch senses. A direct precaution protects their\n  unresolved allocation to bare 拍; it does not make ordinary\n  拍 and 響 synonyms.\n  [律](律.md), [調](調.md) and [整](整.md) retain rhythm or metre\n  senses even when their first displayed meaning concerns something\n  else. A first English label alone cannot settle quiz safety.\n- 字通's independent cheering sense motivates precautions with\n  [勉](勉.md), whose character meanings include encouraging, and\n  [勇](勇.md), which includes cheering up or being in high spirits.\n  Exerting effort, being courageous and applauding are not universally\n  interchangeable. [乗](乗.md) has 乗り のり, rhythm or getting into\n  the spirit, with a kana-preferred qualification in that sense; its\n  direct guard does not depend on the unrelated boarding meaning.\n- The complete 拍手 かしわで entry has a rarely used 拍手 spelling beside\n  柏手. 拍板 びんざさら and 拍板 はくはん are separate instrument\n  entries. Neither whole-word reading establishes 拍 as かしわ or びん.\n- 字通's old-dictionary quotations preserve オフス, a ヒムササラ\n  instrument-name context, ナヅ and ニシル. Their precise historical\n  spelling/sense allocation is not resolved here. They are retained as\n  qualified lookup evidence, not declared invalid or ordinary modern\n  pronunciations.\n- [古](古.md), old, [右](右.md), right, and [川](川.md), river, have\n  independently different lexical ranges, including their secondary\n  nouns and counters; they are not selected merely for different titles.\n\nMetadata: [KANJIDIC2](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/KANJIDIC_Project),\n2026-11-02 snapshot. Words: [JMdict](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/JMdict-EDICT_Dictionary_Project),\nentries 1474820, 2236150, 1583030, 1360940, 1408810, 1841790,\n2257250 and 2257260.\nSupplemental senses and historical forms:\n[Digital Daijisen and 字通, 拍](https://kotobank.jp/word/拍);\n[Weblio's separately attributed dictionary sections](https://www.weblio.jp/content/拍).\nComparison senses: complete\n[JMdict](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/JMdict-EDICT_Dictionary_Project)\nfamilies 1456890, 1532880, 1354720, 1223140, 2228450 and 1487770;\nKANJIDIC2 also retains 勉's encourage and 勇's cheer-up senses.\n",
